The '''RZ-2 A-wing interceptor''', also known as the '''RZ-2 A-wing starfighter''' or the '''Resistance A-wing''', was a wedge-shaped [[starfighter]] manufactured by [[Kuat Systems Engineering]] after the success of the former [[RZ-1 A-wing interceptor]] used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Alliance]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. The RZ-2 incorporated and standardized years of RZ-1 field modifications by the Rebellion, along with making the chassis slimmer and longer to yield even more speed. As such, piloting the ultra-fast yet temperamental starfighter was a matter of pride for various [[Resistance pilot]]s regarding their skills and daring.

==Characteristics==
[[File:RZ2AwingProfile-TLJTOG.png|thumb|left|270px|Their speed and narrow profile made the RZ-2 A-wing a difficult target to hit.]]
The RZ-2 was a single-seat starfighter manufactured by [[Kuat Systems Engineering]]. The ship featured a liquid-cooled flight computer, [[hyperdrive]], [[deflector shield]]ing, and port gyro stabilizer. The two upright stabilizers at the rear of the ship were adjustable for atmospheric flight, and were made of corrugated [[carbo-plas]], a strong but lightweight material. The front of the ship featured a small "slit," which served as a towing slot used to maneuver the craft in hangar or on the ground. Manning the cockpit was room for a single pilot, who was protected by a reinforced canopy augmented with a cockpit deflector shield generator. A cargo storage area in front of the cockpit held survival gear and medical supplies.<ref name="TLJ ICS" />

<div style="float:right">[[File:ConcussionMissile-RSOWM.jpg|thumb|200px|Mission profile typically required concussion missiles]]</div>
For armaments, the ship featured two [[Zija]] [[GO-4 laser cannon]]s attached to a swiveling cannon mount. This allowed pilots to target enemies behind them without having to worry that the finicky mounts would jam in the rear-facing position&mdash;a chronic problem that crippled many Rebel RZ-1s until they returned to base for maintenance. Two concussion missile launchers, fired through depressed exits along both sides of the ship, held enough space to house six missiles per launcher, giving the pilot a total of twelve [[concussion missile]]s to use.<ref name="TLJ ICS" />

Like its RZ-1 predecessor, the RZ-2 was ideal for missions requiring speed: hit-and-run raids, surgical strikes on capital ships, and intelligence-gathering missions. The RZ-2 improved on its predecessors' capabilities, with more powerful sensors for faster data collection and upgraded jammers to impede detection. However, one of the more noticeable changes from the RZ-1 was a streamlined chassis, which not only delivered more speed but also made the starfighter's notoriously sensitive control system slightly more forgiving in flight.<ref name="TLJ ICS" />

==History==
[[File:Awing-RiseoftheResistance.png|thumb|left|250px|An upper aft view of an RZ-2 A-wing]]
The RZ-2 A-wing starfighter rose out of the stunning performance of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] RZ-1 during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. With the original RZ-1 based on Kuat Systems Engineering's original [[R-22 Spearhead]], the company resurrected its forgotten prototype to create the RZ-2<ref name="TLJ ICS" /> as the RZ-1's successor.<ref name="Spark of Rebel">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/news/2018/8/3/spark-of-rebellion-1|text=Spark of Rebellion}}</ref> The RZ-2 incorporated and standardized years of Rebel field modifications, made the chassis slimmer for more speed, and featured generations of improvements to its many systems.<ref name="TLJ ICS" />

The RZ-2 was part of the demilitarized [[New Republic Defense Fleet]] by [[7 ABY|seven years]] after the [[Battle of Yavin]]. Squadrons of the interceptors were deployed aboard the ''[[Tribulan Vort]]'' during the [[Blockade of Substation Grimdock|blockade]] of [[Substation Grimdock]]. They took casualties as they strafed the [[pirate]] warships.<ref name="Last Shot" />

<div style="float:right">[[File:TallissanLintra-SWZ.png|thumb|left|250px|Tallissan Lintra flew an RZ-2 during the evacuation of D'Qar.]]</div>
By the time the RZ-2 was used by the [[Resistance]] during their [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] with the [[First Order]],<ref name="StealthMission" /> it was already decades old.<ref name="TLJ VD">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> With the New Republic cutting A-wing production to a minimum, the Resistance acquired several fighters to be used for everything from reconnaissance patrols to bomber escort missions. As with the previous generation of Rebels, Resistance pilots took pride in proving they had the skills and daring to master the ultra-fast, yet temperamental, starfighter.<ref name="TLJ ICS" />

One notable example of the RZ-2 being used was during the [[Battle of D'Qar|evacuation]] of [[D'Qar]], in which they were [[pilot]]ed by [[Blue Leader]] [[Tallissan Lintra|Tallissan "Tallie" Lintra]]<ref name="Episode VIII" /> and [[Zizi Tlo]].<ref name="TLJ Junior novel">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: A Junior Novel]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The first footage of the RZ-2 A-wing was shown in the [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']] teaser trailer on [[April 14]], [[2017]].<ref name="TLJ teaser">{{SWYouTube|zB4I68XVPzQ|Star Wars: The Last Jedi Official Teaser|sw_url=video/star-wars-the-last-jedi-official-teaser}}</ref> They made their canonical debut, however, in the video game ''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''.<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref>

